docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/issues/49",project,Import silently drops every completed item and exits 0 because it closes without a reason while require_close_reason is on by default
close_reason: "Fixed: runTodoImport now attaches a traceable close reason (Imported as <status> from <file> line <n>) whenever it creates or upserts an item into a terminal status, so checked [x] lines land in the tracker instead of being rejected by the default governance.require_close_reason policy. Partial-import contract chosen: import what it can, then report every dropped line in a structured 'dropped' array on the normal output path (stdout JSON) and set a non-zero process exit code via withDroppedReport (used by the todos importer, todos-import legacy importer, and todos sync). sync refuses to overwrite the source file when the import half dropped a line, preserving the original bytes. Verified by 8 tests (4 end-to-end via real pm subprocess, 4 in-process unit) all run green through pm test --run; release:check passes."
body: ""
